{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/904906-so-which-tribe-is-right","id":904906,"title":"So Which Tribe is Right?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-01T06:18:35-07:00","id":904906,"title":"So Which Tribe is Right?","content":"Each Tribe in Werewolf lists arguments for why <i>its</i> favoured prey is the most dangerous of all. And all of the make fairly good cases. So which one do you think is right? (Discounting the idigam for now).<br /> <br /> Humans have intelligence, technology, versatility, and social systems at their disposal. But careful werewolves can have those things as well, if they're not too proud. Nothing can match humans for numbers, though, and numbers are an advantage that shouldn't be underestimated. From a werewolf perspective, humans are also nearly unmatched at creating secondary problems.<br /> <br /> As werewolves, the Pure can have those advantages too, and turn them against the Blood Talons. Additonally, they can bring anything to take fight that Forsaken can - though the reverse is also largely true, and the Pure are ideologically predictable.<br /> <br /> Spirits are variable, hugely variable, though each one isn't especially versatile. They can have enormous power, but their weaknesses - when you can find them - are usually fairly easy to make use of (at least if you're a Bone Shadow). But where humans and werewolves have known weaknesses, those of spirits can be anything, and you're starting from, if not square one, probably square two, with each one.<br /> <br /> Hosts can vary a lot in power. But they're very hard to get rid of - more than any other threat, they're <i>long term</i>. And if anything beats humans for spawning secondary problems, it's the Hosts.<br /> <br /> The Ridden, especially the Claimed, are an unpredictable mix of humans and spirits - with both the advantages and disadvantages of each, though muted in both cases. And their mentalities take in both natures too, which makes them the hardest to get a handle on.<br /> <br /> <br /> So... by a small margin I'd say the Hunters in Darkness and Storm Lords have the first and second most dangerous, though I'm not sure what order I'd put them in.<br /> <br /> <br /> You?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T07:21:28-07:00","id":904945,"title":"","content":"I'd probably say hosts are the most dangerous of the five tribal sacred prey. They combine aspects of Claimed with their usurping of humans, and werewolves with their being able to affect both sides.<br /> <br /> But most of the spirit examples we're given are more passive threats, with the only really high rank spirit acting in the world being one of the tribal totems. And aside from the Pure, other werewolves aren't made out to be very aggressive either, seemingly wrapped up in their own thing or acting more on a one-on-one skirmishes. Claimed are implied to be uncommon and don't seem to multiply the way hosts do, or often do the damage, though I can see why the Storm Lords would feel they were more of a moral corruption, since they are examples of weakness in mankind.<br /> <br /> When the hosts get out of control they seem to leave entire cities dead in their wake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-01-2016, 10:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T08:00:53-07:00","id":904966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/904906-so-which-tribe-is-right?p=904945#post904945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd probably say hosts are the most dangerous of the five tribal sacred prey. They combine aspects of Claimed with their usurping of humans, and werewolves with their being able to affect both sides.<br /> <br /> But most of the spirit examples we're given are more passive threats, with the only really high rank spirit acting in the world being one of the tribal totems. And aside from the Pure, other werewolves aren't made out to be very aggressive either, seemingly wrapped up in their own thing or acting more on a one-on-one skirmishes. Claimed are implied to be uncommon and don't seem to multiply the way hosts do, or often do the damage, though I can see why the Storm Lords would feel they were more of a moral corruption, since they are examples of weakness in mankind.<br /> <br /> When the hosts get out of control they seem to leave entire cities dead in their wake.</div> </div> </div> </div>In <i>general</i>, I'd say Hosts are the biggest threat most Packs would face. Upon occasion, though, humans can outclass them all (and, in a way, part of the others threat derives <i>from</i> humans).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T08:53:15-07:00","id":904982,"title":"","content":"I think its the a tie beteween human and spirit. These two are so closely interrelated that I don't think its possible to separate them. Humans beget negative spirits, which influence more bad things in people. Claimed are a mix of the two that have the worst aspects of both human and spirit, but weaker in scope. Its a vicious cycle that relies on working together to break out of it.<br /> <br /> Claimed and Pure tend to be symptoms of problems within the spirit world- the Pure want to exalt spirits out of balance, and Claimed are the result of spirits fleeing a poor feeding ground for richer pastures. If not for spirit problems, neither of these would really be an issue, I think. As for Hosts? Their big issue is causinjg problems in the spirit world by messing with the Gauntlet.<br /> <br /> Everything goes back to the spirit-human balance in some way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T09:35:15-07:00","id":905015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/904906-so-which-tribe-is-right?p=904966#post904966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Upon occasion, though, humans can outclass them all (and, in a way, part of the others threat derives <i>from</i> humans).</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. Humans have the power of numbers, but unless you put some supervillains in or play a Countdown to Doomsday scenario, humans aren't really a danger. And mechanically they're the simplest of prey to defeat. On the rare chance you have a hunter cell with silver weapons or something, you're still dealing with the werewolf one-on-one problem. A hunter cell isn't out to destroy an entire city, they're out to kill you.<br /> <br /> We've been slaughtering humans and ghouls in our game, even my character and he has an extreme lack of combat ability. Disregarding the physical superiority werewolves have over humans and that werewolves have access to another world to use for spying, sneak attacks, laying low or retreating. There's suites of abilities that werewolves have that work directly against humans but offer very little in the way of protection or ways to deal with hosts. You can't even pull the 'eat them for aggravated damage' thing on most of the hosts, and they have no banes or bans. They're not just the most dangerous antagonist, they're the ones werewolves are least equipped to deal with, not counting the out of context idigam threat.<br /> <br /> Certainly in a one-on-one scenario or situation where your pack is the target any of the options can be a nasty threat. But hosts represent a more large-scale threat. The fiction throughout the second edition corebook has a pack dealing with beshilu. Thousands of people die, most of the pack is dead and their lives are up-ended, when victory is finally achieved over a a period of years it's because the alpha has sworn to serve a spirit for twenty years to win it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-01-2016, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T10:00:39-07:00","id":905030,"title":"","content":"Bone Shadows. The Bone Shadows are right, spirits are the most dangerous prey.<br /> <br /> A great deal of what makes werewolves dangerous prey is power borrowed from spirits - a werewolf is a deadly combatant, but what kind of foe would he be without his Renown, Rites, or Gifts?<br /> <br /> Humans are only damgerous because of the impact they have on the Shadow ecosystem - one human is no threat at all, but humanity on the whole twists spirits into strange beasts and feeds them tainted Essence.<br /> <br /> The Hosts are dangerous because they manipulate the barrier between flesh and spirit - Shartha are pests, difficult to eradicate, but the real danger they pose is the spirits their gnawing lets in, or the allies their weaving keeps out.<br /> <br /> Claimed are dangerous not only to fight, but in how they transgress the nature of spirit and flesh - what is a Claimed but a spirit that has taken control of its host to blasphemous levels?<br /> <br /> It all comes back to spirits. They may not be the most dangerous prey on their own, but they are what makes the other prey as dangerous as it is.<br /> <br /> Also, don't forget that while Idigam are strange spirits that don't follow the normal rules, at the end of the day, they <i>are</i> spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-01-2016, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T10:28:47-07:00","id":905045,"title":"","content":"Irrelevant discussion is irrelevant. I can ruin your life with any.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T13:15:53-07:00","id":905131,"title":"","content":"All of the Tribes are right.<br /> <br /> All of their favored prey are dangerous enough in the abstract that they cannot be discounted or ranked objectively (the comments about humans above illustrates one of the problems here with viewing &quot;dangerous&quot; solely as &quot;threat in combat&quot; vs. the damage humans do to the local spiritual landscape due to their ignorance and &quot;killing them&quot; doesn't actually help this).<br /> <br /> As such you can only consider one more dangerous than another in the context of a local area (aka in the context of what the ST and players choose to highlight in their personal games).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T15:13:45-07:00","id":905214,"title":"","content":"Ah, what is the most dangerous game?<br /> <br /> Currently, whatever's behind me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T06:43:54-07:00","id":905588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/904906-so-which-tribe-is-right?p=905030#post905030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bone Shadows. The Bone Shadows are right, spirits are the most dangerous prey<br /> <br /> &lt;Snip a good case&gt;.</div> </div> </div> </div>You make a good case.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T07:32:04-07:00","id":905617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/904906-so-which-tribe-is-right?p=905588#post905588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You make a good case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! Honestly, I think similarly strong cases can be made for each of the other prey, depending on how you define dangerous. But I ultimately have to concede that even if you go in for a different brand of dangerous, spirits are at least the most pervasive prey, and many of the other prey are as dangerous as they are specifically because of how they interact with spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T07:42:35-07:00","id":905629,"title":"","content":"Iron Masters are right of course.<br /> <br /> For all the admittedly great dangers spirits, Hosts, Ridden, and other Uratha pose.. humanity is the source of the impetus, sustenance, methods of interaction, and reproductive processes of all these other enemies. Human's warp the shadow like literally no other force in the Hisil, which in turn generates the greatest influxes of Essence. Hosts and spirits both require, more or less humans to gain potent and useful hosts to further their goals. Sure they are needed to continue the species, but just as Forsaken cleave to the humans, so do the Pure ( though I'm assuming the Ivory Claws now are more incestuous now there is no true danger of mating with their own kind aside from a potential &quot;masquerade&quot; breach in the form of a potent Wolf-blooded) - thus the Pure are unlikely to just die off. And let us not forget that there might be hundreds of thousands, maybe even a million or more werewolves.. they still a minority compared to the billions of humans.. to say nothing of our superior military might and our weaponry. Even without silver, an Uratha isn't going to take more than a few rounds from a M-60 unless they are in Gauru form, and even then, it's an unfair fight even with Lunacy and insane regenerative abilities ( and the other fun bits.) Sure, one or even ten ordinary people are no threat usually... but when it comes down to it.. the children of Father Wolf are not the apex predators as a species, and they never will be again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T07:55:41-07:00","id":905638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/904906-so-which-tribe-is-right?p=905030#post905030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bone Shadows. The Bone Shadows are right, spirits are the most dangerous prey.<br /> <br /> A great deal of what makes werewolves dangerous prey is power borrowed from spirits - a werewolf is a deadly combatant, but what kind of foe would he be without his Renown, Rites, or Gifts?<br /> <br /> Humans are only damgerous because of the impact they have on the Shadow ecosystem - one human is no threat at all, but humanity on the whole twists spirits into strange beasts and feeds them tainted Essence.<br /> <br /> The Hosts are dangerous because they manipulate the barrier between flesh and spirit - Shartha are pests, difficult to eradicate, but the real danger they pose is the spirits their gnawing lets in, or the allies their weaving keeps out.<br /> <br /> Claimed are dangerous not only to fight, but in how they transgress the nature of spirit and flesh - what is a Claimed but a spirit that has taken control of its host to blasphemous levels?<br /> <br /> It all comes back to spirits. They may not be the most dangerous prey on their own, but they are what makes the other prey as dangerous as it is.<br /> <br /> Also, don't forget that while Idigam are strange spirits that don't follow the normal rules, at the end of the day, they <i>are</i> spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is basically the premise of 1e, and why keeping spirits under control was the crux of the setting.<br /> <br /> Which is to say, it's no longer so cut and dried.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T08:01:23-07:00","id":905641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/904906-so-which-tribe-is-right?p=905617#post905617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks! Honestly, I think similarly strong cases can be made for each of the other prey, depending on how you define dangerous. But I ultimately have to concede that even if you go in for a different brand of dangerous, spirits are at least the most pervasive prey, and many of the other prey are as dangerous as they are specifically because of how they interact with spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see it the same, only reverse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T08:12:37-07:00","id":905651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/904906-so-which-tribe-is-right?p=905641#post905641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see it the same, only reverse.</div> </div> </div> </div>That spirits are only as dangerous as they are because of the other prey? Yeah, that's the flip side to the bone shadow argument, and definitely a valid take.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T08:13:22-07:00","id":905653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/904906-so-which-tribe-is-right?p=905638#post905638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" cl